WEBVTT


00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.500
Downloaded @ subs4free.club


00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:54.879
You deserve this...


00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:57.679
You do.


00:01:57.840 --> 00:02:00.239
You've earned it.


00:03:16.040 --> 00:03:20.239
I can do all things. All things.


00:03:36.880 --> 00:03:38.279
Come on...


00:03:38.440 --> 00:03:41.719
Come on, come on...


00:06:14.160 --> 00:06:16.839
I am the Invigilator.


00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:18.959
Listen carefully
to every word I say.


00:06:19.120 --> 00:06:21.919
There will be no repetition.


00:06:22.080 --> 00:06:26.039
I won't apologise for the hardships
you've endured reaching this room


00:06:26.200 --> 00:06:29.679
'cause the pressures
and pains were necessary.


00:06:29.840 --> 00:06:32.759
Resilience is a key
attribute in these dark times,


00:06:32.920 --> 00:06:37.439
and if you can't survive our selection
process, you won't survive in the job.


00:06:37.600 --> 00:06:41.439
Many highly-qualified
candidates tried to get this far and failed.


00:06:41.600 --> 00:06:44.319
You have succeeded.


00:06:44.480 --> 00:06:46.599
And now the final stage lies before you.


00:06:46.920 --> 00:06:50.319
One last hurdle
separates you from your goal -


00:06:50.480 --> 00:06:52.839
which is to join our esteemed ranks.


00:06:53.000 --> 00:06:55.879
The test is simple
in comparison, yet it will determine


00:06:56.040 --> 00:06:59.399
who leaves this room
with a contract of employment


00:06:59.560 --> 00:07:03.479
and who leaves
with the bus fare home.


00:07:04.960 --> 00:07:07.999
Through these trials,
you've gained some idea of the power


00:07:08.160 --> 00:07:10.919
of this organisation,
so believe me when I tell you


00:07:11.080 --> 00:07:14.959
that there's no law
in this room but our law.


00:07:15.360 --> 00:07:19.359
And the only rules
in here are our rules.


00:07:21.600 --> 00:07:25.119
There's one question before you,
and one answer is required.


00:07:25.280 --> 00:07:28.239
If you try
to communicate with myself


00:07:28.400 --> 00:07:32.159
or the guard,
you will be disqualified.


00:07:32.320 --> 00:07:36.799
If you spoil your paper,
intentionally or accidentally,


00:07:36.960 --> 00:07:39.079
you will be disqualified.


00:07:39.240 --> 00:07:42.959
If you choose
to leave the room for any reason,


00:07:43.120 --> 00:07:45.159
you will be disqualified.


00:07:47.000 --> 00:07:48.719
Any questions?


00:07:51.680 --> 00:07:54.479
Best of luck, ladies and gentlemen.


00:07:56.920 --> 00:08:00.079
We're giving the eight of you
80 minutes.


00:08:01.880 --> 00:08:06.639
80 minutes to convince us
you have what it takes to join us.


00:08:06.800 --> 00:08:11.159
80 minutes to determine
the next 80 years of your lives.


00:08:13.080 --> 00:08:15.279
Begin.


00:10:02.440 --> 00:10:05.239
I'm not finished.


00:10:05.400 --> 00:10:09.839
No, please. You can't!
This isn't a proper test!


00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:13.319
Please, I'll start over!
Just give me a chance!


00:11:33.680 --> 00:11:35.959
Hey...


00:11:36.120 --> 00:11:37.959
Listen, listen, listen, listen.


00:11:41.920 --> 00:11:45.799
It's not about what he said,
you know.


00:11:45.960 --> 00:11:48.559
It's what he didn't say.


00:11:52.560 --> 00:11:54.959
"lf you attempt to communicate..."


00:11:55.120 --> 00:11:57.599
..with myself or the guard...


00:11:57.760 --> 00:11:59.959
..you will be disqualified.


00:12:04.400 --> 00:12:07.479
- He didn't say...
- ..we can't speak to each other.


00:12:09.680 --> 00:12:14.719
- Now you're talking.
- Is this the ultimate mind-fuck or what?


00:12:22.960 --> 00:12:26.319
- Has anyone figured out the answer?
- No.


00:12:26.480 --> 00:12:28.839
It's not about the answer.
It's about the question.


00:12:29.000 --> 00:12:33.039
- What's the question?
- We've got 74 minutes left to figure out.


00:12:33.200 --> 00:12:35.679
If the answer
takes one minute to write down.


00:12:35.840 --> 00:12:37.519
If it takes 73 minutes to write,


00:12:37.680 --> 00:12:40.919
we have one minute
to guess the question.


00:12:41.080 --> 00:12:44.399
We're short on writing space.
I'm betting it's the former.


00:12:44.560 --> 00:12:46.999
We've gotta help each other.


00:12:47.160 --> 00:12:50.999
We're in competition.
Why should I help you to beat me?


00:12:51.160 --> 00:12:54.519
We may be in competition
to answer the question,


00:12:54.680 --> 00:12:58.159
but to establish the question
we have to cooperate.


00:12:58.320 --> 00:13:00.279
They expect us to cooperate, don't they?


00:13:00.440 --> 00:13:02.759
What'd you expect,
you're gonna win this job,


00:13:02.920 --> 00:13:06.279
with all the rewards that come with it,


00:13:06.440 --> 00:13:08.959
by giving them
a little simple written answer?


00:13:09.120 --> 00:13:11.839
Facts and opinions?
Compare and contrast (!)


00:13:12.000 --> 00:13:14.639
They're not looking for that.


00:13:14.800 --> 00:13:18.479
A job like this needs initiative,


00:13:18.640 --> 00:13:20.559
observation...


00:13:22.840 --> 00:13:24.519
..interplay.


00:13:24.680 --> 00:13:29.719
- Teamwork. He's right.
- We're in a stress scenario.


00:13:29.880 --> 00:13:33.199
A confusing, time-critical situation


00:13:33.360 --> 00:13:37.079
designed to test our intelligence,
and resilience.


00:13:37.240 --> 00:13:40.719
- To bring out the worst in us.
- Or the best.


00:13:42.400 --> 00:13:44.999
We help each other until
the playing field is open


00:13:45.160 --> 00:13:48.719
then it's every man for themselves -
no offence, girls.


00:13:51.640 --> 00:13:54.159
- Are we all agreed?
- Yes.


00:13:54.320 --> 00:13:56.919
Agreed.


00:14:00.920 --> 00:14:05.359
- Let's go, Gandhi.
- My name isn't Gandhi, friend. It's...


00:14:05.520 --> 00:14:09.959
No names. Not real ones, anyway.
They're not written on this for a reason.


00:14:10.920 --> 00:14:12.719
We'll use nicknames, then.


00:14:14.160 --> 00:14:19.079
- All right, let's make this easy.
- We already have numbers.


00:14:19.240 --> 00:14:21.119
Yeah, and visual.


00:14:25.640 --> 00:14:27.759
You're Black.


00:14:29.200 --> 00:14:31.079
I'm White.


00:14:31.240 --> 00:14:33.359
You're Brown.


00:14:35.160 --> 00:14:37.039
We've got Blonde here,


00:14:37.200 --> 00:14:39.719
Brunette there...


00:14:42.120 --> 00:14:44.279
..Dark, I suppose.


00:14:46.720 --> 00:14:48.999
And last
as well as least we've got Deaf.


00:14:56.360 --> 00:14:59.759
- Tough last round.
- Yeah, whatever.


00:15:02.280 --> 00:15:04.119
Any objections?


00:15:04.280 --> 00:15:08.079
Apart from your grossly insensitive
sexual and racial stereotyping?


00:15:08.240 --> 00:15:10.759
If you're the sensitive type,
you shouldn't be here, love.


00:15:10.920 --> 00:15:13.079
I'll take Brown over Gandhi,


00:15:13.240 --> 00:15:16.679
we're talking about
something that matters.


00:15:17.640 --> 00:15:19.439
I'll take that as a yes.


00:15:30.920 --> 00:15:33.559
So, what else hasn't he forbidden?


00:15:37.440 --> 00:15:40.679
He hasn't forbidden
us to stand, has he?


00:16:08.880 --> 00:16:14.159
- Well, l guess moving about is OK too.
- What's that gonna achieve?


00:16:14.320 --> 00:16:17.719
I don't know, Brown. But sitting
wasn't getting us anywhere exciting.


00:16:17.880 --> 00:16:21.799
What if the question is written down
but we just can't see it?


00:16:21.960 --> 00:16:24.039
That's what l'm talking about!


00:16:24.200 --> 00:16:27.719
- You mean like invisible ink?
- Or a watermark.


00:16:27.880 --> 00:16:31.199
- It's possible.
- It's probable. Where else would it be?


00:16:31.360 --> 00:16:35.599
We'd need something
to reveal it. Like light.


00:16:42.480 --> 00:16:47.879
- Right.
- Those are halogen.


00:16:48.040 --> 00:16:50.839
Those aren't.


00:16:53.280 --> 00:16:56.119
They won't bite, you know.


00:17:06.080 --> 00:17:08.599
They're not gonna make it
that easy, are they?


00:17:08.760 --> 00:17:11.919
We're on the clock.
How hard can they afford to make it?


00:17:15.160 --> 00:17:19.319
What if the pencil
isn't just for writing the answer?


00:17:19.480 --> 00:17:23.999
What if it reveals the question too?
By shading the page, like tracing paper?


00:17:25.000 --> 00:17:29.039
- Try it, Blonde.
- No. Remember what he said.


00:17:29.200 --> 00:17:32.679
If you spoil your paper,
intentionally or accidentally...


00:17:32.840 --> 00:17:35.519
..you'll be disqualified.


00:17:35.680 --> 00:17:41.319
Is anyone certain they know
what his definition of spoiling is?


00:17:41.480 --> 00:17:44.759
Look, let's crack this.
Throw out some ideas.


00:17:44.920 --> 00:17:47.959
What if the questions are hidden
in the paper,


00:17:48.120 --> 00:17:51.719
but each of us has to write
a different answer? He said...


00:17:51.880 --> 00:17:55.639
There's one question before you,
and one answer is required.


00:17:55.800 --> 00:17:58.719
That doesn't mean it's
the same question for each of us.


00:17:58.880 --> 00:18:01.639
There could be eight different
questions and answers.


00:18:01.800 --> 00:18:05.079
If we find one question,
we can find them all.


00:18:05.240 --> 00:18:08.559
Not necessarily.
Not if our eight individual questions


00:18:08.720 --> 00:18:11.799
can only be revealed
using eight different methods.


00:18:11.960 --> 00:18:13.839
Perhaps we're not
meant to cooperate at all.


00:18:14.000 --> 00:18:15.439
I like that idea.


00:18:15.600 --> 00:18:18.519
Or there's only one question,
printed on only one of our sheets.


00:18:18.680 --> 00:18:22.359
- Then we'd need to cooperate...
- Time-out for some testing.


00:18:24.120 --> 00:18:27.559
- Everyone up to the light.
- I said it won't be that easy.


00:18:27.720 --> 00:18:30.639
Unless you want to make a list
of our brainwaves, White,


00:18:30.800 --> 00:18:33.399
I say we cross a few off as we go.


00:18:35.480 --> 00:18:37.039
Fine.


00:19:01.960 --> 00:19:04.519
Allow me.


00:19:12.760 --> 00:19:15.039
Thank you.


00:19:21.920 --> 00:19:23.919
Yeah, join in any time, Deaf (!)


00:19:32.000 --> 00:19:34.119
Not one for small talk, are you?


00:19:34.280 --> 00:19:35.759
Come.


00:19:38.160 --> 00:19:40.199
Relax, you'll get it back (!)


00:19:48.960 --> 00:19:54.399
Like l said, l think we can
strike light off the list.


00:19:58.480 --> 00:20:01.719
Light is a spectrum.


00:20:01.880 --> 00:20:03.919
There's light we can see,


00:20:04.080 --> 00:20:06.519
but there's light we can't see.


00:20:06.680 --> 00:20:09.639
Like ultraviolet, infra-red, X-rays.


00:20:09.800 --> 00:20:12.479
If we can't see it,
how are we supposed to find it?


00:20:12.640 --> 00:20:16.199
The source must be visible,
even if the light isn't. Right?


00:20:43.920 --> 00:20:45.919
Find the light switches.


00:20:53.840 --> 00:20:57.159
There aren't any,
not in here anyway. And...


00:20:57.320 --> 00:20:59.879
If you choose to leave
the room for any reason...


00:21:00.040 --> 00:21:01.359
..we'll be disqualified.


00:21:03.560 --> 00:21:05.959
There must be some way
to trigger these.


00:21:09.520 --> 00:21:11.519
This is emergency lighting.


00:21:11.680 --> 00:21:13.799
So let's create an emergency.


00:21:15.480 --> 00:21:17.599
That would be very risky.


00:21:17.760 --> 00:21:20.919
- It's less risky than doing nothing.
- He's right.


00:21:21.080 --> 00:21:25.999
If we try this and fail,
we can't go back. Blackout.


00:21:31.640 --> 00:21:33.479
We vote.


00:22:02.800 --> 00:22:05.279
Those too.


00:22:33.400 --> 00:22:36.279
Nice! Very nice!


00:22:36.440 --> 00:22:38.439
Touch of blue, what you wanted?


00:22:38.600 --> 00:22:40.399
This is black light.


00:22:40.560 --> 00:22:43.919
The kind credit card firms
use to reveal their security symbols.


00:22:53.240 --> 00:22:55.919
Shame we didn't apply
to work for Visa (!)


00:22:56.080 --> 00:22:59.799
- Our gamble might have paid off.
-  lt did pay off.


00:22:59.960 --> 00:23:03.239
Just not in the way you wanted.


00:23:03.400 --> 00:23:06.599
You acted, and the room reacted.


00:23:06.760 --> 00:23:10.999
We've entered a dialogue now,
we should keep going.


00:23:11.160 --> 00:23:14.079
Yeah, maybe... Maybe not.


00:23:17.000 --> 00:23:20.479
Sorry, it was invisible
light you said you wanted.


00:23:20.640 --> 00:23:22.879
This looks pretty
fucking visible to me.


00:23:23.040 --> 00:23:26.959
Scientific term for it
is "near-ultraviolet".


00:23:27.120 --> 00:23:29.919
It didn't work,
but it was worth trying.


00:23:32.120 --> 00:23:35.159
If nothing else we'll
come out of this with great tans.


00:23:37.440 --> 00:23:39.439
We've got to knock these out too.


00:23:41.160 --> 00:23:43.879
The top halves
of these strips aren't lit.


00:23:44.040 --> 00:23:47.199
Look.


00:24:10.800 --> 00:24:13.519
Infrared. The other option.


00:24:13.680 --> 00:24:17.599
- That exposes something too?
- It's less common than UV, but yes.


00:24:18.800 --> 00:24:21.239
Art historians use it
to make reflectograms


00:24:21.400 --> 00:24:24.199
of the sketch outlines
beneath paintings.


00:24:24.360 --> 00:24:27.719
If there's a hidden
layer in our papers...


00:24:34.680 --> 00:24:37.559
Carefully.


00:25:04.000 --> 00:25:05.799
Let me guess, "near-infrared"?


00:25:07.000 --> 00:25:09.119
All right, everyone, try again.


00:25:18.520 --> 00:25:22.079
- Anyone? Anything?
- No.


00:25:22.240 --> 00:25:25.399
- Shit!


00:25:28.240 --> 00:25:32.399
- Now can we get off the lighting?
- If you can provide a better alternative.


00:25:32.560 --> 00:25:35.879
Any alternative. We've burned
a quarter of our time already.


00:25:37.960 --> 00:25:41.639
Perhaps they company's Japanese-owned
and this is an origami exam.


00:25:41.800 --> 00:25:44.319
Be our guest.
That sheet is yours to spoil.


00:25:48.360 --> 00:25:53.279
Yes, it is, but only your sheet.


00:26:02.480 --> 00:26:06.039
- It's a piece of paper.
- No, it's more than that now.


00:26:06.200 --> 00:26:09.279
This is experimental material.


00:26:09.440 --> 00:26:11.719
- If you spoil...
- ..your paper.


00:26:11.880 --> 00:26:15.639
- Your paper!
- ..you will be disqualified.


00:26:15.800 --> 00:26:17.399
This isn't mine. This is hers.


00:26:17.560 --> 00:26:19.959
"It's not fair" (!)


00:26:20.120 --> 00:26:23.079
And she's gone. So...


00:26:29.040 --> 00:26:36.319
Tracing...


00:26:40.640 --> 00:26:44.199
Well, congratulations, Blonde.
Your idea sucks too.


00:26:44.360 --> 00:26:46.999
This could all be
a distraction, you know.


00:26:47.160 --> 00:26:49.119
We could be missing
something obvious.


00:26:49.280 --> 00:26:51.159
Yeah, yeah, yeah! All right!


00:26:51.320 --> 00:26:56.559
Light does not work,
lead does not work...


00:26:57.880 --> 00:26:59.679
Liquid!


00:27:01.400 --> 00:27:03.799
Oh, yeah...


00:27:08.960 --> 00:27:11.679
Right.


00:27:11.840 --> 00:27:14.439
Lick it, spit on it, get it wet.


00:27:14.600 --> 00:27:18.079
If the question's watermarked
we need some liquid to bring it out.


00:27:18.240 --> 00:27:20.919
- What are you doing with yours?
- You don't wanna know.


00:27:21.080 --> 00:27:23.799
- Actually, we do.
- Well, you can come and watch.


00:27:23.960 --> 00:27:26.119
You can hold it for me
too if you like.


00:27:26.280 --> 00:27:30.159
- Though I'd prefer it if Blonde did.
- That's disgusting.


00:27:30.320 --> 00:27:33.159
"By any means necessary",
right, brother?


00:27:33.320 --> 00:27:35.519
- If we can do it, we should.


00:27:35.680 --> 00:27:39.719
That's not gonna burn the question out.
Urine's sterile. You can drink it...


00:27:39.880 --> 00:27:44.479
- Wish you would.
- Great. A pissing contest.


00:27:51.840 --> 00:27:53.839
Anything?


00:27:55.240 --> 00:27:59.559
- I can't tell yet. lt's all yellow.
- Hold it up and let us see.


00:27:59.720 --> 00:28:01.839
If you'll lend me a glove, l'll oblige.


00:28:03.160 --> 00:28:05.119
Well, l'm running out of ideas.


00:28:12.560 --> 00:28:15.639
Giving up so easily, Black,
with 57 minutes on the clock?


00:28:15.800 --> 00:28:17.279
You know what...


00:28:17.440 --> 00:28:20.999
Will you two shut up?
Some of us are trying to think!


00:28:32.760 --> 00:28:35.079
At last, he speaks.


00:28:40.200 --> 00:28:44.479
He's French.


00:28:44.640 --> 00:28:48.279
- Vous voyez la?
- Does anyone here speak French?


00:28:48.440 --> 00:28:50.119
Vous voyez la?


00:28:52.760 --> 00:28:54.759
Can you see?


00:28:54.920 --> 00:28:57.719
Vous voyez...?


00:29:01.120 --> 00:29:03.439
Regardez bien.


00:29:03.600 --> 00:29:08.519
- Can you see it in there?
- See what in there?


00:29:08.680 --> 00:29:12.479
See what? Pretty colours?


00:29:12.640 --> 00:29:15.999
- Vous-meme.
- Yourself.


00:29:17.040 --> 00:29:19.039
Vous vous voyez.


00:29:21.080 --> 00:29:23.679
It shows you yourself.


00:29:28.520 --> 00:29:31.999
- And then there was six.
- Leave him alone. He's done nothing.


00:29:32.160 --> 00:29:35.399
He's done nothing for me either
or any of us. Nutter!


00:29:37.320 --> 00:29:41.519
Toujours y voir clairement est primordial.


00:29:41.680 --> 00:29:43.199
To see clearly is all.


00:29:43.360 --> 00:29:46.279
All right, that's enough
out of you, Sartre!


00:29:49.600 --> 00:29:51.479
Fucking philosophers.


00:29:53.280 --> 00:29:57.399
Thank God this world
belongs to the doers, not the thinkers.


00:29:58.800 --> 00:30:02.359
Since we're proposing grand theories,
let me advance one of my own.


00:30:04.080 --> 00:30:07.319
This is not an exam.


00:30:08.640 --> 00:30:10.719
Not in the conventional sense anyway.


00:30:10.880 --> 00:30:13.359
Look around.


00:30:13.520 --> 00:30:15.959
You couldn't ask for a more
representative group


00:30:16.120 --> 00:30:18.879
to qualify for the final stage.


00:30:19.280 --> 00:30:22.239
Four men and four women
entered this room,


00:30:22.400 --> 00:30:25.319
all from differing cultures
and ethnic backgrounds,


00:30:25.480 --> 00:30:28.439
possessing a healthy mixture
of skill-sets.


00:30:28.600 --> 00:30:32.039
How convenient that is. How staged.


00:30:32.200 --> 00:30:37.039
What are you saying? They rigged
the tests to bring us together?


00:30:37.200 --> 00:30:39.879
Some kind of experiment
in group dynamics.


00:30:40.040 --> 00:30:44.559
- What are you on about?
- I'm saying this is a game.


00:30:44.720 --> 00:30:48.319
- And they're betting on us.
- Right and who is "they"?


00:30:49.320 --> 00:30:51.479
The board.


00:30:56.880 --> 00:30:59.399
I guess they're watching us right now.


00:31:02.600 --> 00:31:05.999
They'll be ex-VCs mostly.


00:31:06.160 --> 00:31:08.639
Probably left
the incubator when they realised


00:31:08.800 --> 00:31:11.679
their little start-up
had struck the motherlode.


00:31:11.840 --> 00:31:14.559
It wouldn't get any sweeter
than this, l'm sure.


00:31:14.720 --> 00:31:17.719
So they joined the board,


00:31:17.880 --> 00:31:19.959
secured some big fat stock options


00:31:20.120 --> 00:31:23.599
and bought themselves
the right to have a little fun...


00:31:23.760 --> 00:31:25.719
With us.


00:31:25.880 --> 00:31:28.759
Don't they have better things to do
with their time?


00:31:31.120 --> 00:31:33.439
Like what?


00:31:33.600 --> 00:31:36.719
At their level, money ceases
to be the prime motivator.


00:31:36.880 --> 00:31:38.879
It's risk they live for.


00:31:39.040 --> 00:31:41.239
They're type A's, like us,


00:31:41.400 --> 00:31:44.559
and just as they were trained
by their investment companies,


00:31:44.720 --> 00:31:47.639
they're still betting on ideas today.


00:31:47.800 --> 00:31:51.199
Ours.


00:31:51.360 --> 00:31:55.719
Who'll decipher the question,
who'll come up empty and fold


00:31:55.880 --> 00:31:59.279
and who'll crack under pressure?


00:32:02.160 --> 00:32:03.479
You could be wrong.


00:32:03.640 --> 00:32:06.359
It could just be
the Invigilator behind there.


00:32:06.520 --> 00:32:09.079
Wanna bet?


00:32:10.360 --> 00:32:12.279
l wouldn't, if l were you.


00:32:12.440 --> 00:32:15.679
Brown talks like a gambler
because he is one.


00:32:15.840 --> 00:32:18.879
A professional. Aren't you?


00:32:21.240 --> 00:32:24.879
And you, Dark, are a shrink.


00:32:29.400 --> 00:32:33.839
Psychologist or psychiatrist?
I forget the difference.


00:32:34.000 --> 00:32:36.319
Psychiatrists dispense drugs
to control mood.


00:32:36.480 --> 00:32:38.839
I'm a qualified student
of human behaviour.


00:32:39.000 --> 00:32:41.639
Then you should know
what I'm talking about.


00:32:41.800 --> 00:32:46.679
The point of having power
is to exercise it in all its forms.


00:32:46.840 --> 00:32:50.279
- We're pawns of the Gods in here.
- So? This changes nothing!


00:32:50.440 --> 00:32:51.759
Yeah...


00:32:51.920 --> 00:32:55.559
Games are played to be won...
as a team.


00:32:55.720 --> 00:32:57.999
Yeah, or as individuals.


00:32:58.160 --> 00:33:01.319
Not if the only way for them
to win is for us to lose.


00:33:01.480 --> 00:33:04.439
All of us.
Have you thought about that?


00:33:07.080 --> 00:33:08.839
You're wrong.


00:33:09.000 --> 00:33:11.359
There is no 'them' watching us.


00:33:11.520 --> 00:33:14.359
The CEO is hands-on.


00:33:14.520 --> 00:33:17.959
He micro-manages anything
of importance to his company.


00:33:18.120 --> 00:33:21.679
And this is no ordinary
selection process.


00:33:21.840 --> 00:33:24.759
We're special.


00:33:24.920 --> 00:33:28.999
If anyone's back there
besides the lnvigilator, it's him.


00:33:29.160 --> 00:33:33.279
Everyone else is a secretary
in his structure - even board members.


00:33:33.440 --> 00:33:36.399
That's how he likes it.


00:33:38.280 --> 00:33:40.039
How do you know all this?


00:33:40.520 --> 00:33:42.079
We're wasting time.


00:33:42.240 --> 00:33:44.999
There's 50 minutes left,
we're no closer to finding the question.


00:33:45.160 --> 00:33:49.039
Somehow l suspect
my question relates to the question.


00:33:49.200 --> 00:33:51.919
So answer me.


00:33:52.080 --> 00:33:56.719
- How did you learn that information?
- Same way you learned about the board.


00:33:56.880 --> 00:34:00.519
I don't know anything about the board.
I made an educated guess.


00:34:00.680 --> 00:34:04.359
But you...you know who the CEO is
and what he's like. How come?


00:34:04.520 --> 00:34:08.239
- How come you don't?
- How could we? We were headhunted.


00:34:10.040 --> 00:34:12.959
- Why? Weren't you?
- Of course not!


00:34:13.120 --> 00:34:17.719
I heard there was a vacancy and applied.
I thought we all did!


00:34:18.280 --> 00:34:21.399
Are you saying you wanna work
for this company,


00:34:21.560 --> 00:34:26.519
jumped through every hoop to get here
but you don't know who they are?


00:34:26.680 --> 00:34:30.759
They listed salary and benefits.
The job description detailed,


00:34:30.920 --> 00:34:34.079
"A high level of responsibility
in a Fortune 500 company


00:34:34.240 --> 00:34:39.239
manufacturing state-of-the-art technology
in a core service industry". All right?


00:34:39.400 --> 00:34:42.999
- You didn't wanna know anymore?
- The deal was no questions asked.


00:34:43.160 --> 00:34:46.199
Anyone would've done
the same in our position...


00:34:46.360 --> 00:34:48.679
Anyone with...balls.


00:34:52.160 --> 00:34:54.439
- You all applied?
- Yeah.


00:34:56.160 --> 00:34:59.319
If this job is so prestigious,
why they need to advertise?


00:34:59.480 --> 00:35:02.279
- They didn't.
- We have our sources.


00:35:02.440 --> 00:35:06.199
- Looks like we're outnumbered.
- I wouldn't cry about it.


00:35:06.360 --> 00:35:08.919
- You've the edge over us now.
- How's that?


00:35:09.080 --> 00:35:12.079
You're wanted, aren't you?
They invited you to apply.


00:35:13.880 --> 00:35:17.719
I'd say we're disadvantaged because
you showed the initiative to apply.


00:35:17.880 --> 00:35:19.879
We're behind the curve now.


00:35:20.040 --> 00:35:25.759
So tell us what you know,
starting with a complete job description.


00:35:25.920 --> 00:35:28.999
- We don't have that information.
- Should we believe that?


00:35:29.160 --> 00:35:31.439
We don't know any more about the job.


00:35:31.600 --> 00:35:34.199
We just know about the company
and, believe me,


00:35:34.360 --> 00:35:37.959
the worst job with them
beats the best anyone else can offer.


00:35:38.120 --> 00:35:43.039
He's right. Who they are,
who the CEO is and what he's achieved,


00:35:43.200 --> 00:35:45.399
that's all you need to know.


00:35:45.560 --> 00:35:47.279
All right, so tell us about it.


00:35:50.720 --> 00:35:52.959
I'll give you a clue.


00:35:53.120 --> 00:35:56.479
1 0 years ago a lot of healthy
young people around the world


00:35:56.640 --> 00:35:59.039
got sick and started dying.


00:35:59.200 --> 00:36:00.879
You may have read about that.


00:36:01.040 --> 00:36:05.199
Then a medical researcher
patented a virus suppressant.


00:36:05.360 --> 00:36:07.999
The mortality rate
halved in six months,


00:36:08.160 --> 00:36:10.639
and now his company
is the biggest player


00:36:10.800 --> 00:36:14.199
in the global health industry
with a turnover of $20 billion


00:36:14.360 --> 00:36:17.679
and a market
capitalisation of $60 billion.


00:36:17.840 --> 00:36:19.199
If it was a nation state,


00:36:19.360 --> 00:36:22.719
it would rank as
the world's eighth largest economy.


00:36:22.880 --> 00:36:24.919
Next year that rises to sixth.


00:36:25.920 --> 00:36:27.799
You may have read about that too.


00:36:29.720 --> 00:36:31.719
Biorg!


00:36:31.880 --> 00:36:33.479
80 minutes...


00:36:33.640 --> 00:36:36.439
..to determine the next
80 years of your lives.


00:36:36.600 --> 00:36:37.879
Remember?


00:36:38.040 --> 00:36:40.479
Longevity is what they do.


00:36:40.640 --> 00:36:46.159
Antisense drugs, gene therapy,
microsurgical applications.


00:36:46.320 --> 00:36:49.799
They announced a hiring freeze
last year! Everyone knows that.


00:36:49.960 --> 00:36:55.919
Publicly that's true.
Privately...they're expanding again.


00:36:57.320 --> 00:37:00.119
Gearing up for a big push of some kind.


00:37:02.240 --> 00:37:04.319
They've found a cure.


00:37:04.480 --> 00:37:06.639
They must have!


00:37:06.800 --> 00:37:09.559
Manufacturing and marketing


00:37:09.720 --> 00:37:13.199
would triple in size for the roll-out.


00:37:14.440 --> 00:37:17.559
There'd be jobs for all of us!


00:37:17.720 --> 00:37:21.559
- We don't know that.
- But it's possible, isn't it?


00:37:23.240 --> 00:37:26.759
How long would
FDA approval take, if it's true?


00:37:26.920 --> 00:37:30.399
- That's not my field.
- Hold on.


00:37:30.560 --> 00:37:34.199
Why are you so interested?
Something you want to tell us?


00:37:34.360 --> 00:37:37.879
If you're asking "Am I infected?",
White, the answer is "No".


00:37:38.040 --> 00:37:41.999
- I'm clean.
- But someone you know isn't.


00:37:42.160 --> 00:37:45.719
We all know someone with the virus,
that's why they call it a pandemic.


00:37:45.880 --> 00:37:50.359
Nice evasive manoeuvre, but we're talking
about the real reason you're here.


00:37:52.040 --> 00:37:54.519
Yeah...
So, what relative is it?


00:37:54.680 --> 00:37:59.239
Is it your mum? Your dad?
Little sister...


00:37:59.400 --> 00:38:02.079
It's my partner, OK?
He can't afford suppressants,


00:38:02.240 --> 00:38:05.479
but they're discounted to employees -
are you happy now?


00:38:07.840 --> 00:38:09.919
So who else is a charity case here?


00:38:13.320 --> 00:38:15.879
Yeah, you wouldn't speak up, if you were.


00:38:16.040 --> 00:38:19.639
Don't want to commit career suicide
on camera like she just has.


00:38:19.800 --> 00:38:21.759
With a little help from you.


00:38:21.920 --> 00:38:24.319
I didn't create her situation,
I just exposed it.


00:38:24.480 --> 00:38:29.079
Doesn't matter. lf she gets
the answer right, she's still hired.


00:38:29.240 --> 00:38:32.279
Really? Says who?
What...them?


00:38:34.280 --> 00:38:39.119
- If memory serves me correct...
- The only rules in here are our rules.


00:38:39.280 --> 00:38:42.079
They can disqualify everyone!


00:38:42.240 --> 00:38:45.599
They can do whatever they like
and we can't do a thing about it.


00:38:45.760 --> 00:38:47.759
So...congratulations!


00:38:47.920 --> 00:38:51.119
You've just disqualified yourself
without breaking any rules.


00:38:51.280 --> 00:38:54.799
He won't kick you out,
but you're dead in the water, honey.


00:38:56.280 --> 00:38:58.279
Dead in the water.


00:38:59.120 --> 00:39:01.679
Don't listen to him.
We'll get through this together.


00:39:01.840 --> 00:39:04.119
Thanks, but I don't need your help,


00:39:04.280 --> 00:39:08.519
because my situation
isn't a weakness, it's a strength.


00:39:10.880 --> 00:39:13.799
I'm sure they're
smart enough to realise that.


00:39:13.960 --> 00:39:17.079
And if l could talk to the CEO


00:39:17.240 --> 00:39:21.239
I'd assure him the treatment my partner
needs will only deepen my commitment


00:39:21.400 --> 00:39:24.719
to his organisation for years to come.


00:39:28.560 --> 00:39:30.559
You really think he's behind there?


00:39:30.720 --> 00:39:33.359
He's lived behind walls for years.


00:39:33.520 --> 00:39:37.319
No one outside his inner circle
has even seen him since the lPO.


00:39:38.640 --> 00:39:41.199
If he wanted to hire an assistant,


00:39:41.360 --> 00:39:43.799
this is the way he'd do it.


00:39:57.880 --> 00:39:59.639
What are you doing?


00:39:59.800 --> 00:40:03.119
Proving my worth. You may have
run out of ideas, but I haven't.


00:40:03.280 --> 00:40:07.759
- Don't even try talking to him.
- I'm not gonna talk to him.


00:40:17.720 --> 00:40:20.199
Is there anything in there,
or is he happy to see you?


00:40:42.960 --> 00:40:45.599
What have we here?


00:40:49.200 --> 00:40:51.119
Is that all?


00:40:55.800 --> 00:40:57.119
Heat may have an effect


00:40:57.280 --> 00:40:59.919
if the papers have been
chemically treated.


00:41:00.080 --> 00:41:04.639
- If we warmed them from beneath...
- It's not heat and chemicals, Black.


00:41:06.200 --> 00:41:07.999
It's just chemicals.


00:41:11.000 --> 00:41:14.479
What are you talking about? H2O?


00:41:16.200 --> 00:41:19.159
We already tried H2O!
It's in all our bodily fluids!


00:41:19.320 --> 00:41:24.239
What are these pipes connected to?
You could pump any liquid through them!


00:41:28.240 --> 00:41:30.999
Come on, Einstein


00:41:31.160 --> 00:41:34.199
Good Lord, you're right.


00:41:38.440 --> 00:41:41.279
These aren't infrared at all.


00:41:41.440 --> 00:41:44.799
They're safelights!
Common standard-issue safelights!


00:41:44.960 --> 00:41:48.399
We're in a darkroom!
This room is a great big darkroom!


00:41:48.560 --> 00:41:52.719
- And this must be photographic paper.
- Meaning we can develop it?


00:41:52.880 --> 00:41:56.799
You hope... Developing photos
isn't a one-stage process.


00:41:56.960 --> 00:42:00.879
- It takes chemical baths, fixing agents...
- For colour photography.


00:42:01.040 --> 00:42:03.359
To pull black letters
from a white background


00:42:03.520 --> 00:42:05.239
all you need is developing fluid.


00:42:09.360 --> 00:42:10.839
Let's do this.


00:42:16.040 --> 00:42:17.879
I'm in.


00:42:21.920 --> 00:42:25.279
Even if she's right,
isn't a chemical shower a bad idea?


00:42:25.440 --> 00:42:28.239
It'll be diluted.
They wouldn't hire damaged goods.


00:42:28.400 --> 00:42:31.279
But covering your eyes,
nose and mouth may be wise.


00:42:32.320 --> 00:42:35.079
They're not the
only things worth covering.


00:42:39.920 --> 00:42:42.479
That's it: join in at last.


00:42:42.640 --> 00:42:44.719
You're deaf but not dumb, eh?


00:43:19.920 --> 00:43:22.239
No worries, love. Let me.


00:43:33.120 --> 00:43:35.039
Let's go.


00:44:05.480 --> 00:44:08.359
- Well?
- It'll take a few moments.


00:44:55.320 --> 00:44:56.839
Where's my paper?


00:45:00.920 --> 00:45:03.239
Has anyone seen my paper?


00:45:17.600 --> 00:45:21.079
No!


00:45:27.120 --> 00:45:31.039
You bastard! Bastard!


00:45:31.200 --> 00:45:35.239
How could you?
How could you? Bastard!


00:46:07.160 --> 00:46:09.439
What did you just do?


00:46:10.600 --> 00:46:14.319
What l had to.


00:46:14.480 --> 00:46:16.719
I should punch your lights out!


00:46:19.720 --> 00:46:23.999
- Black, what did you do?
-  lt's not what he did.


00:46:24.160 --> 00:46:26.839
- lt's what he said.
- What?


00:46:27.000 --> 00:46:30.319
"Lights out".
So...lights up!


00:46:37.040 --> 00:46:41.319
- That's better.
- Lights out.


00:46:41.480 --> 00:46:46.599
Lights up. Voice-activated.


00:46:46.760 --> 00:46:52.079
- They're playing with us.
- Great, isn't it?


00:46:52.240 --> 00:46:56.719
- Everybody watch what you say.
- And do.


00:47:32.000 --> 00:47:34.599
Up one minute, down the next.


00:47:39.320 --> 00:47:43.119
Can't write on this
anymore, can you? Go on, try.


00:47:45.840 --> 00:47:48.679
Don't then.


00:47:52.880 --> 00:47:57.039
Are you hungry, mate?
Oi, are you hungry?


00:47:58.520 --> 00:48:00.759
I am. l'm really hungry.


00:48:00.920 --> 00:48:03.919
There's no snack machines
in here, though, are there?


00:48:05.840 --> 00:48:09.599
Go on, rip it up...
Oi! Rip it up!


00:48:10.040 --> 00:48:14.679
- Hey! What did l tell you before?
- She said leave him alone, White.


00:48:21.880 --> 00:48:24.479
- Tear it up!
- White, will you stop!


00:48:24.640 --> 00:48:28.159
Tear it up! Tear it!


00:48:31.320 --> 00:48:33.919
I won't tell you again, White!


00:48:34.080 --> 00:48:37.799
That's it, good boy. Go on.


00:48:39.440 --> 00:48:42.119
Go on. More, more.


00:48:43.080 --> 00:48:45.079
Put it in your mouth.


00:49:00.960 --> 00:49:05.919
S'il vous plait!


00:49:15.520 --> 00:49:18.119
And then there were five.


00:49:22.480 --> 00:49:26.239
- "Bastard" doesn't do you justice.


00:49:27.400 --> 00:49:30.039
You said we should cooperate
until we discovered the question!


00:49:30.200 --> 00:49:32.159
So l lied!


00:49:32.320 --> 00:49:35.279
I lied. So what?


00:49:35.440 --> 00:49:38.319
Lying is not against the rules, is it?


00:49:40.200 --> 00:49:45.279
Anyway, you don't have to listen to me,
let alone agree or obey.


00:49:45.440 --> 00:49:49.679
You should thank me.
All of you should thank me.


00:49:49.840 --> 00:49:53.439
I've just narrowed down the field,
so your odds improve.


00:49:53.600 --> 00:49:56.439
Odds mean nothing without
the question in front of us!


00:49:56.600 --> 00:49:59.639
You can forget about
any more help from us in finding it.


00:49:59.800 --> 00:50:03.079
I don't need your help.
You'll find it's you who needs my help.


00:50:03.240 --> 00:50:05.759
You know why?
'Cause I figured it out.


00:50:05.920 --> 00:50:07.999
Oh, really? The question?
What is it, then?


00:50:08.160 --> 00:50:09.799
Why should I?


00:50:10.800 --> 00:50:14.039
Because if you don't,
I'll beat it out of you.


00:50:16.480 --> 00:50:20.959
You're full of shit, White.
You have been from the start.


00:50:21.120 --> 00:50:23.119
You don't know anything.


00:50:23.280 --> 00:50:26.479
He wouldn't tell us if he did,
'cause he's a narcissist.


00:50:26.640 --> 00:50:29.039
He despises us.


00:50:29.200 --> 00:50:31.719
Sticks and stones, love.


00:50:32.840 --> 00:50:35.159
I bet you say that to all the boys.


00:50:35.320 --> 00:50:37.839
Only the ones with
Narcissistic Personality Disorder.


00:50:38.000 --> 00:50:41.119
There are nine character traits
to look for:


00:50:41.280 --> 00:50:44.719
arrogance, grandiosity,
a belief in one's uniqueness,


00:50:44.880 --> 00:50:47.239
a preoccupation
with power and success,


00:50:47.400 --> 00:50:50.599
an excessive need to be admired,
a sense of entitlement,


00:50:50.760 --> 00:50:54.799
lack of empathy and the twin tendencies
to envy and exploit others.


00:50:54.960 --> 00:50:58.479
For clinical diagnosis,
a patient must exhibit five of these.


00:50:58.640 --> 00:51:02.359
- You tick enough boxes.
- You can add a tenth to that list.


00:51:02.520 --> 00:51:06.839
"A tendency to see through all the bullshit
surrounding you, and rise above it."


00:51:07.000 --> 00:51:10.719
- I'll tick that box myself.
- Let me tick it for you.


00:51:23.120 --> 00:51:25.959
- That was smart.
- That was necessary.


00:51:26.120 --> 00:51:28.399
We may need him. He's a resource.


00:51:28.560 --> 00:51:30.999
You don't like someone? Outwit them.


00:51:31.160 --> 00:51:33.719
He's an enemy of the group,
and a distraction!


00:51:43.360 --> 00:51:45.159
Are you gonna give me a hand?


00:51:52.520 --> 00:51:54.879
- One, two...


00:52:04.800 --> 00:52:06.199
What are you doing?


00:52:06.360 --> 00:52:11.079
Ensuring that he can't cause
any more trouble when he wakes up.


00:52:11.240 --> 00:52:14.439
- And taking him out of the game.
- That hardly seems fair.


00:52:14.600 --> 00:52:18.079
He's sacrificed his right to fair treatment.
Forward a bit.


00:52:26.000 --> 00:52:31.359
See? I put him down
and suddenly we're cooperating again.


00:52:45.080 --> 00:52:47.519
He's a talker.


00:52:52.760 --> 00:52:55.039
We could go further than this.


00:52:56.560 --> 00:52:58.559
She's right.


00:52:58.720 --> 00:53:02.959
We could carry him
to the door and slide him out.


00:53:05.760 --> 00:53:08.759
He ejected two of us:
why shouldn't we eject him?


00:53:08.920 --> 00:53:13.719
- Call it justice, or karma if you prefer.
- You don't believe in forgiveness?


00:53:13.880 --> 00:53:17.879
- I'll forgive him afterwards.
- And your gospel of cooperation?


00:53:19.320 --> 00:53:23.599
I'll tolerate anyone, except the intolerant.


00:53:26.680 --> 00:53:28.519
Those in favour...


00:53:33.440 --> 00:53:35.439
Fifty-fifty.


00:53:35.600 --> 00:53:37.519
To each his own.


00:53:42.880 --> 00:53:46.559
If you won't think selflessly
about this, think selfishly.


00:53:46.720 --> 00:53:48.399
The Invigilator said...


00:53:48.560 --> 00:53:51.439
If you choose to leave this room
for any reason,


00:53:51.600 --> 00:53:53.519
you'll be disqualified.


00:53:53.680 --> 00:53:57.159
He's not choosing to leave, is he?
You're choosing for him.


00:53:59.280 --> 00:54:02.239
Which puts you at risk too.


00:54:24.280 --> 00:54:28.599
Go on, White, spoil yourself.
It's your turn.


00:54:29.560 --> 00:54:31.959
Make your mark.


00:54:38.160 --> 00:54:42.439
Look, we have less than half an hour left
and we still don't know the question.


00:54:42.600 --> 00:54:46.479
He claims to know the question.


00:54:56.720 --> 00:54:59.879
- Shut up!


00:55:13.040 --> 00:55:15.319
I need medication, it's in my pocket.


00:55:15.480 --> 00:55:19.839
- What kind of medication?
- What does it matter?


00:55:20.000 --> 00:55:23.559
A pill, all right? l need to take
it every hour, on the hour.


00:55:23.720 --> 00:55:26.999
- That's right now.
- Every hour, on the hour?


00:55:27.160 --> 00:55:30.119
Only one condition is treated that way.


00:55:33.760 --> 00:55:35.559
You're infected too, aren't you?


00:55:39.520 --> 00:55:42.759
That's more than justice.
That's poetic justice.


00:55:42.920 --> 00:55:46.439
If you don't believe me,
untie my arms, so I can take the pill!


00:55:47.760 --> 00:55:49.919
- Go on!
- Nice try.


00:55:50.080 --> 00:55:52.919
It's pathetic, actually.


00:55:53.080 --> 00:55:57.799
Take it yourself. Get it for me yourself.
It's in my left pocket!


00:55:57.960 --> 00:56:02.119
- I'll do what you want. Just do it.
- Really?


00:56:02.280 --> 00:56:05.079
Tell us what the question is then.


00:56:06.320 --> 00:56:08.479
All right, get the pill and l'll tell you.


00:56:08.640 --> 00:56:10.759
Come on! Fucking do it!


00:56:12.120 --> 00:56:14.559
Go on, it's my left pocket.


00:56:14.720 --> 00:56:16.999
Go on, try again, it's in there. Go on.


00:56:19.200 --> 00:56:21.159
Where the fuck is it?


00:56:21.320 --> 00:56:24.479
One of you has taken it!
One of you has fucking taken it!


00:56:25.320 --> 00:56:29.559
This isn't funny! You know what happens
when you don't take suppressants!


00:56:29.720 --> 00:56:34.479
Unconsciousness. Convulsions.
Shock. Coma. Then death.


00:56:35.720 --> 00:56:37.159
We know exactly what happens


00:56:37.320 --> 00:56:39.919
and the process takes hours,
not minutes.


00:56:45.120 --> 00:56:48.679
Listen, mate,
I'll be out of this for good!


00:56:48.840 --> 00:56:50.479
A taste of your own medicine.


00:56:51.800 --> 00:56:57.559
- Don't do it, don't do it.
- Look on the bright side, brother (!)


00:56:57.720 --> 00:57:01.879
If you start to convulse,
we'll know you're telling the truth.


00:57:02.040 --> 00:57:04.679
Then we'll gladly help you.


00:57:12.320 --> 00:57:14.759
Looks like you've got your wish.


00:57:17.720 --> 00:57:20.479
For now.


00:57:20.640 --> 00:57:23.679
He had to be dealt with
one way or another.


00:57:23.840 --> 00:57:26.839
I wouldn't be surprised
if he was a plant all along.


00:57:27.000 --> 00:57:31.079
It's the kind of thing they'd do
to stir up our internal dynamics.


00:57:31.240 --> 00:57:33.279
To set us against one another.


00:57:33.440 --> 00:57:36.839
If so, we've seized back the initiative.


00:57:37.000 --> 00:57:39.719
Or you have.


00:57:41.880 --> 00:57:43.799
He isn't smart enough to be a plant.


00:57:45.600 --> 00:57:48.879
But you on the other hand.


00:57:49.040 --> 00:57:51.039
You think she's one of them?


00:57:51.200 --> 00:57:53.759
Don't be absurd!
I told you l'm a psychologist!


00:57:53.920 --> 00:57:58.399
You claimed to be a qualified
student of psychology, not a practitioner.


00:58:00.360 --> 00:58:04.679
I've studied psychology too,
and reverse psychology.


00:58:04.840 --> 00:58:07.759
What better way to hide
your true role in this farce


00:58:07.920 --> 00:58:10.759
than to accuse another
candidate of playing your part?


00:58:10.920 --> 00:58:12.799
I don't know what you're talking about.


00:58:12.960 --> 00:58:15.759
Amateur psychology
is a useful tool for gamblers,


00:58:15.920 --> 00:58:18.599
but a degree in the subject


00:58:18.760 --> 00:58:24.479
sounds like the perfect foundation
for a career in, say human resources.


00:58:25.760 --> 00:58:28.039
You're on the wrong side
of the glass.


00:58:28.200 --> 00:58:31.439
- He's the one who manipulated...
- Maybe you work as a team.


00:58:31.600 --> 00:58:34.279
He's got the mouth, but you...


00:58:34.440 --> 00:58:38.199
..know an awful lot
about Biorg Pharmaceuticals.


00:58:38.360 --> 00:58:41.159
- I told you l applied!
- So did we.


00:58:41.320 --> 00:58:43.999
- And l do my research!
- So did we!


00:58:45.520 --> 00:58:48.759
Any of us could be plants,
but not all of us.


00:58:48.920 --> 00:58:52.199
At least one candidate has
to be genuine for the test to be viable.


00:58:52.360 --> 00:58:54.119
- That would be me.
- And me.


00:58:54.280 --> 00:58:58.239
My point is we can't prove
anyone's guilt or innocence,


00:58:58.400 --> 00:59:00.199
so it's a waste of time to try.


00:59:00.360 --> 00:59:02.959
If we can't maintain trust
and cooperation, we're through.


00:59:03.120 --> 00:59:05.439
Trust has to be earned, sister.


00:59:05.600 --> 00:59:08.879
We never had cause to trust
each other in the first place.


00:59:09.040 --> 00:59:13.559
Trust is a choice. We can choose
to keep cooperating, if necessary.


00:59:13.720 --> 00:59:16.559
- I think it's necessary.
- We have no other option.


00:59:16.720 --> 00:59:18.639
Trust makes me nervous.


00:59:20.720 --> 00:59:25.319
- I prefer proof.
- What are you doing?


00:59:25.480 --> 00:59:27.799
- Get off me!
- Are you insane?


00:59:27.960 --> 00:59:32.399
- Brown, why are you doing this?
- Because I like winning!


00:59:38.560 --> 00:59:40.839
Now tell us the truth, Dark.


00:59:41.000 --> 00:59:44.199
Please...
You said we've to trust each other!


00:59:44.360 --> 00:59:47.519
Now you're gonna stand there
while he interrogates me?


00:59:51.200 --> 00:59:53.559
Looks like it. They wanna know too.


00:59:55.120 --> 00:59:57.159
Further denials will only waste time.


00:59:57.320 --> 01:00:02.599
Confess and l'll release you. I promise.


01:00:14.120 --> 01:00:17.199
OK, I work for them,
but they didn't put me in here!


01:00:17.360 --> 01:00:20.679
I heard about the job internally
and applied like everyone else!


01:00:20.840 --> 01:00:23.399
Not everyone.


01:00:27.040 --> 01:00:29.879
Tell us what we want to know.


01:00:30.040 --> 01:00:33.799
I can't tell you anything because
I don't know anything!


01:00:33.960 --> 01:00:37.839
HR doesn't cover the CEO's office,
he hires his staff personally!


01:00:38.000 --> 01:00:42.599
I'm not lying!
I wanna step up as badly as you do!


01:00:42.760 --> 01:00:47.239
Like l said,
trust is a devalued currency in here.


01:00:47.400 --> 01:00:50.959
What proof can I possibly give you?


01:01:11.840 --> 01:01:14.639
You know, it's funny...


01:01:14.800 --> 01:01:18.079
how something so simple
and inoffensive


01:01:18.240 --> 01:01:20.599
as a piece of paper,


01:01:20.760 --> 01:01:24.559
when placed in the wrong hands


01:01:24.720 --> 01:01:27.239
can become a deadly weapon.


01:01:29.040 --> 01:01:32.079
All from one slice of a tree.


01:01:35.320 --> 01:01:38.599
- What are you doing?
- What has to be done.


01:01:38.760 --> 01:01:41.279
You're gonna torture me?


01:01:41.440 --> 01:01:44.759
- Do something! Please!
- Brown, what are you doing?


01:01:44.920 --> 01:01:48.119
- I know what l'm doing.
- You've done this before?


01:01:48.280 --> 01:01:50.999
- In the services.
- I thought you were a gambler.


01:01:51.160 --> 01:01:53.279
All soldiers are gamblers.


01:01:53.440 --> 01:01:58.279
See, l find the flesh
of the inner thigh especially sensitive.


01:01:58.440 --> 01:02:03.039
- Fuck you! Get off me!
- Stop this! This can't be our only option!


01:02:03.200 --> 01:02:06.959
No, it isn't, it's mine.


01:02:09.640 --> 01:02:12.599
What have we here?


01:02:15.280 --> 01:02:17.919
Seems you got there before me.


01:02:18.080 --> 01:02:22.279
What, undervalued at work and at home?


01:02:23.840 --> 01:02:25.839
Daddy didn't love you, hm?


01:02:26.000 --> 01:02:29.039
You studied psychology to find out why?
Tell me I'm wrong.


01:02:29.200 --> 01:02:33.199
On second thoughts, don't answer that.
Answer this...


01:02:33.360 --> 01:02:37.559
- What is the question?
- I don't know!


01:02:37.720 --> 01:02:39.799
- You're lying!
- I don't know, I swear!


01:02:39.960 --> 01:02:42.439
What is the question?


01:02:42.600 --> 01:02:44.599
What is the purpose of this exam?


01:02:44.760 --> 01:02:48.799
Would I volunteer if the only way for you
to solve this was to beat it out of me?


01:02:48.960 --> 01:02:50.959
How fucked up are you?


01:02:52.720 --> 01:02:55.959
With 20 minutes left, this fucked up.


01:02:56.120 --> 01:02:57.919
- OK, enough!


01:03:02.120 --> 01:03:05.079
Don't interfere.


01:03:09.960 --> 01:03:12.919
For God's sake. This is a woman.


01:03:17.360 --> 01:03:19.719
Equal opportunities, Black.


01:03:19.880 --> 01:03:22.919
HR wouldn't expect anything less,
would they?


01:03:24.760 --> 01:03:27.359
Oh, by all means, ask him for help.


01:03:27.520 --> 01:03:29.079
Look, it's nothing personal.


01:03:29.240 --> 01:03:32.639
We just need to know what you know.


01:03:32.800 --> 01:03:37.799
Brown, don't do this!
There must be another way!


01:03:37.960 --> 01:03:39.919
We need certainty.


01:03:40.080 --> 01:03:43.519
The kind only unbearable pain can give...


01:03:47.320 --> 01:03:49.879
I've told you everything I know!


01:03:50.040 --> 01:03:52.599
Please stop!


01:03:55.640 --> 01:03:58.439
..or the threat of it.


01:04:01.360 --> 01:04:04.039
She's telling the truth.


01:04:10.680 --> 01:04:13.519
Sorry.


01:04:25.040 --> 01:04:28.839
Here.


01:04:29.000 --> 01:04:32.559
Thank you.


01:05:19.960 --> 01:05:23.959
You wanted convulsions -
now you've got them.


01:05:30.920 --> 01:05:33.999
You think he's faking it.


01:05:34.160 --> 01:05:36.759
It's genuine.


01:05:36.920 --> 01:05:42.879
- How do you know?
- My wife, she died from it.


01:05:45.440 --> 01:05:48.439
I'm a carrier. He's not faking.


01:05:50.320 --> 01:05:52.879
Even liars tell the truth occasionally.


01:05:55.040 --> 01:05:58.479
- He really needs that pill, doesn't he?
- Fast.


01:06:00.760 --> 01:06:03.559
If anyone took it, own up now.


01:06:09.080 --> 01:06:13.839
All right, if we can't trust each other,
we'll have to search each other.


01:06:51.480 --> 01:06:54.159
Nothing.


01:07:04.760 --> 01:07:08.599
- Got any gum?
- Sorry. l'm all out.


01:07:11.080 --> 01:07:14.199
Really?


01:07:22.960 --> 01:07:26.679
All soldiers are gamblers


01:07:26.840 --> 01:07:29.399
and all gamblers are cheats, l've found.


01:07:29.560 --> 01:07:32.599
Given the opportunity.


01:07:32.760 --> 01:07:35.639
- I took a calculated risk.
- You're as bad as he is.


01:07:35.800 --> 01:07:38.839
No, he's worse. There was
never any pretence about White.


01:07:40.560 --> 01:07:43.559
- Let's think about it selfishly again.
- While he's dying?


01:07:43.720 --> 01:07:45.599
That's not selfishness, that's murder!


01:07:45.760 --> 01:07:49.199
Coma comes before death, right?
People recover from comas.


01:07:49.360 --> 01:07:51.879
Not this kind. Sink too deep
and it's irreversible.


01:07:52.040 --> 01:07:55.079
But that pill mimics
an adrenaline shot to the heart.


01:07:55.240 --> 01:07:59.239
- If you're gonna do it, do it now.
- Forgotten what you said about him?


01:07:59.400 --> 01:08:01.799
We're not releasing him
We're saving his life!


01:08:01.960 --> 01:08:05.039
I'm afraid I can't do that!


01:08:14.720 --> 01:08:16.759
I can see it, but l can't reach!


01:08:16.920 --> 01:08:19.079
Let me try!


01:08:26.400 --> 01:08:28.959
Obviously the Gods
agree with my risk assessment.


01:08:38.040 --> 01:08:40.039
Is he unconscious?


01:08:40.200 --> 01:08:43.519
He's lapsing!


01:08:43.680 --> 01:08:45.639
We have to carry him out for treatment.


01:08:47.880 --> 01:08:49.839
Biorg will understand. Trust me.


01:08:50.000 --> 01:08:52.599
Are you gonna help me?


01:08:55.920 --> 01:08:58.999
Fine, you can live with his death
on your consciences. I can't.


01:09:09.080 --> 01:09:12.319
He's bleeding! What does that mean?


01:09:12.480 --> 01:09:16.039
I don't know: l haven't seen
this before. But it can't be good.


01:09:26.480 --> 01:09:30.559
- Do something, Black!
- Like what? I'm not a doctor!


01:09:30.720 --> 01:09:33.319
Help him, please!


01:09:33.480 --> 01:09:36.079
Can't you see he's dying?


01:09:39.160 --> 01:09:43.639
No! I work for you! I work here!


01:10:16.240 --> 01:10:19.039
You weren't wrong about that pill.


01:10:25.200 --> 01:10:26.879
Hey...


01:10:28.040 --> 01:10:30.439
- If you can hear me, nod your...
- Fuckers.


01:10:42.160 --> 01:10:44.399
I have it too, brother.


01:10:44.560 --> 01:10:48.199
Yeah, well, don't expect me to thank you.


01:10:49.480 --> 01:10:51.999
You have her to thank...


01:10:52.160 --> 01:10:53.599
..not me.


01:11:00.360 --> 01:11:02.679
Well, l would've preferred the kiss of life.


01:11:02.840 --> 01:11:06.199
I bet you're good at that.


01:11:10.040 --> 01:11:12.719
Wow.


01:11:12.880 --> 01:11:15.359
Four down and four to go.


01:11:17.240 --> 01:11:19.119
And only 10 minutes on the clock.


01:11:21.640 --> 01:11:24.639
Exciting (!)


01:11:29.480 --> 01:11:32.799
I felt you take it, you know.


01:11:32.960 --> 01:11:36.399
Room not big enough for both of us?


01:11:44.200 --> 01:11:47.439
That's the spirit, Brown.


01:11:56.560 --> 01:11:59.079
If you remember me taking it,


01:11:59.240 --> 01:12:03.159
you'll remember
the promise you made us.


01:12:03.320 --> 01:12:05.399
Blonde gave you the pill as requested.


01:12:05.560 --> 01:12:08.559
Now give us what we asked for in return.


01:12:10.120 --> 01:12:12.799
- The question?
- What is it?


01:12:12.960 --> 01:12:16.279
Where is it?


01:12:16.440 --> 01:12:19.479
You still don't get it, do you?


01:12:22.880 --> 01:12:25.879
Let me spell this out for you.


01:12:29.080 --> 01:12:32.399
There is no question!


01:12:34.040 --> 01:12:37.599
All right?


01:12:37.760 --> 01:12:40.919
There never was one!


01:12:41.080 --> 01:12:43.879
Not the kind you're looking for anyway.


01:12:44.040 --> 01:12:47.039
That's what you've been holding back?


01:12:47.200 --> 01:12:50.839
- That's your big secret?
- Uh-huh.


01:12:51.000 --> 01:12:52.799
You heard the lnvigilator.


01:12:52.960 --> 01:12:56.359
There's one question before you,
and one answer is required.


01:12:56.520 --> 01:12:58.679
There is one question!
You're calling him a liar?


01:12:58.840 --> 01:13:04.399
When you've eliminated the impossible,
whatever's left has to be the truth.


01:13:05.640 --> 01:13:08.559
No matter how crazy it seems.


01:13:11.520 --> 01:13:14.719
This test is the question!


01:13:16.480 --> 01:13:18.399
And the answer is us.


01:13:20.360 --> 01:13:24.559
- We're the answers.
- Answers, plural?


01:13:24.720 --> 01:13:27.639
- If l recall...
- One answer is required.


01:13:27.800 --> 01:13:30.999
- Singular.
- That's right.


01:13:32.680 --> 01:13:35.759
Just one of us.


01:13:42.280 --> 01:13:43.999
You wouldn't dare.


01:13:50.560 --> 01:13:51.959
Whoa! Whoa!


01:13:53.320 --> 01:13:57.079
- Whoa! Everybody calm down.
- Seconded.


01:13:57.240 --> 01:14:00.639
All right, all right, all right.


01:14:04.960 --> 01:14:08.879
- You're not gonna shoot me.
- I didn't take it to shoot you!


01:14:09.040 --> 01:14:12.479
I took it to stop you
from using it on us!


01:14:15.240 --> 01:14:17.039
Let me tell you what I think.


01:14:18.000 --> 01:14:22.479
I think we're the answers too.
All of us together, as a team!


01:14:22.640 --> 01:14:24.839
I think we'd
all passed when we walked in.


01:14:25.000 --> 01:14:27.719
All each of us can do
is lose what we've already won


01:14:27.880 --> 01:14:30.359
through selfishness,
stupidity and impatience!


01:14:34.120 --> 01:14:36.839
Deaf was right.


01:14:37.000 --> 01:14:39.999
We see what we want to see in here.


01:14:40.160 --> 01:14:42.399
You're a fighter
so you all can think about


01:14:42.560 --> 01:14:44.159
is being the last man standing,


01:14:44.320 --> 01:14:47.839
but they never said
there was only one position available.


01:14:48.000 --> 01:14:50.159
Yeah, l see what l want to see, Black.


01:14:52.680 --> 01:14:55.119
And you hear what you want to hear.


01:14:55.280 --> 01:14:57.479
But answer me this, brother (!)


01:14:57.640 --> 01:15:02.519
What corporation doesn't know
how many positions it's got available?


01:15:02.680 --> 01:15:07.839
What CEO can't decide whether he wants
one assistant or eight?


01:15:11.160 --> 01:15:14.879
There's only one job going
in his office, you know that?


01:15:15.040 --> 01:15:17.999
And the rest is fantasy.


01:15:23.640 --> 01:15:26.039
White, stay back!


01:15:26.200 --> 01:15:28.359
This ain't worth killing for.


01:15:28.520 --> 01:15:31.039
You seem to think it is.
Is it...


01:15:33.040 --> 01:15:36.879
- ..worth dying for?
- Put the gun down, Black.


01:15:38.760 --> 01:15:40.599
You started this, now it's in play!


01:15:40.760 --> 01:15:43.479
- We can't put it back.
- Throw it out the door.


01:15:43.640 --> 01:15:46.519
That won't break any rules.


01:15:49.200 --> 01:15:52.239
Go on, then, shoot me.


01:15:52.400 --> 01:15:56.079
Go on, shoot me in the head, go on.


01:16:00.520 --> 01:16:03.759
- See? You can't fight who you are.
- Don't!


01:16:48.320 --> 01:16:50.999
Fingerprint ID.


01:16:54.480 --> 01:16:57.119
No!


01:16:59.480 --> 01:17:02.039
OK.


01:17:06.240 --> 01:17:07.999
OK, OK.


01:17:09.800 --> 01:17:11.959
Just tell us what you want.


01:17:12.120 --> 01:17:15.679
I want to be alone!


01:17:15.840 --> 01:17:18.879
You want us to spoil our papers?


01:17:19.040 --> 01:17:21.479
Disqualify ourselves?


01:17:23.360 --> 01:17:24.839
OK.


01:17:25.880 --> 01:17:29.039
We'll take those odds
over the alternative.


01:17:31.520 --> 01:17:34.039
You win.


01:17:40.160 --> 01:17:43.999
I can't let my partner escort you out,
we just became friends.


01:17:49.000 --> 01:17:52.239
How about you walk out instead?


01:17:52.400 --> 01:17:55.319
Each of you. One by one.


01:17:57.000 --> 01:17:59.719
Starting with you.


01:18:01.400 --> 01:18:03.759
Come on, we ain't got all day! Let's go.


01:18:16.440 --> 01:18:18.799
They deserve you.


01:18:24.240 --> 01:18:25.719
Now you.


01:18:32.720 --> 01:18:34.639
Come on.


01:18:37.280 --> 01:18:40.359
- Don't be stupid, Black.
- You won't shoot.


01:18:41.920 --> 01:18:43.999
I'll be missed.


01:18:45.320 --> 01:18:47.599
You're sick like me.


01:18:47.760 --> 01:18:51.719
Your death will be explained away, OK?


01:18:51.880 --> 01:18:55.239
No one outside this room even cares.


01:18:55.400 --> 01:18:59.759
They've got problems of their own,
like avoiding the infection themselves.


01:19:01.200 --> 01:19:03.879
Your conscience will haunt you.


01:19:05.600 --> 01:19:07.959
You're assuming l've got one.


01:19:11.440 --> 01:19:13.999
I'll go. I'm through with this.


01:19:17.800 --> 01:19:19.279
(Ready?)


01:19:28.960 --> 01:19:30.439
Don't cry, darlin'.


01:19:30.600 --> 01:19:34.119
You were a passenger in here, anyway.


01:19:34.280 --> 01:19:38.039
- You fucked your way to the top.
- Then l saved your life.


01:19:40.480 --> 01:19:43.119
Well, anyone can make a mistake.


01:19:49.600 --> 01:19:51.599
Lights out!


01:19:56.840 --> 01:19:58.879
Lights on!


01:21:31.880 --> 01:21:34.639
Toujours y voir clairement
est primordial.


01:21:34.800 --> 01:21:36.799
To see clearly is all.


01:21:52.520 --> 01:21:53.999
Well?


01:21:55.920 --> 01:22:00.519
You said there's one answer
and you're looking at him!


01:22:01.440 --> 01:22:05.359
I've done everything!
I made everything happen in here,


01:22:05.520 --> 01:22:07.519
and she's done nothing!


01:22:08.480 --> 01:22:11.199
It's me! l'm the one you want!


01:22:11.360 --> 01:22:13.559
I'M THE ONE YOU WANT!


01:22:51.760 --> 01:22:55.959
If you try to communicate
with myself or the guard...


01:22:57.520 --> 01:22:59.959
..you will be disqualified.


01:23:09.960 --> 01:23:12.439
That's it, join in at last.


01:23:12.600 --> 01:23:15.239
You're deaf but not dumb, eh?


01:25:40.240 --> 01:25:44.599
There is one question before you,
and one answer is required.


01:26:26.880 --> 01:26:29.959
- Answers?
- That's what you've been holding back?


01:26:30.120 --> 01:26:34.679
- That's your big secret?
- You still don't get it, do you?


01:26:34.840 --> 01:26:36.799
What is it? Where is it?


01:26:36.960 --> 01:26:39.559
- The question?
- What's the purpose of this exam?


01:26:39.720 --> 01:26:44.039
- The question? What is it? Tell us!
- What does it matter?


01:26:44.200 --> 01:26:47.039
You really think
he's behind there?


01:26:47.200 --> 01:26:49.919
He's lived behind walls for years.


01:26:50.080 --> 01:26:52.159
How do you know all this?


01:26:52.320 --> 01:26:56.079
Are you saying that they rigged
the test to bring us all together?


01:26:57.480 --> 01:26:59.479
Is there something you want to tell us?


01:26:59.640 --> 01:27:02.479
- lt's a piece of paper.
- It's more than that.


01:27:02.640 --> 01:27:05.199
lf we can't see it,
how are we supposed to find it?


01:27:05.360 --> 01:27:08.959
What if the question
is written down? We just can't see it?


01:27:09.120 --> 01:27:11.479
What if it reveals
the question too?


01:27:11.640 --> 01:27:13.959
They're not gonna
make it that easy.


01:27:14.120 --> 01:27:16.639
How hard
can they afford to make it?


01:27:18.280 --> 01:27:20.719
So has anyone
figured out the answer yet?


01:27:20.880 --> 01:27:24.759
lt's not about the answer,
it's about the question.


01:27:25.920 --> 01:27:28.079
What is the question?


01:27:41.800 --> 01:27:44.719
What is the question?


01:28:00.360 --> 01:28:03.319
Any questions?


01:28:06.760 --> 01:28:08.279
No.


01:28:09.720 --> 01:28:14.359
That's the answer you wanted
to the first question asked of us.


01:28:14.520 --> 01:28:16.879
The only question asked of you.


01:28:19.120 --> 01:28:22.399
- I almost missed it too.
- Almost.


01:28:22.560 --> 01:28:25.399
As it is, we're happy
to be hiring someone today.


01:28:26.440 --> 01:28:28.359
I haven't accepted yet.


01:28:28.520 --> 01:28:31.679
You wouldn't have participated
if you didn't want the job.


01:28:31.840 --> 01:28:35.279
That was before. Before all this.


01:28:37.560 --> 01:28:40.279
Now it's over, I have questions.


01:28:40.440 --> 01:28:43.839
- Questions?
- More than one.


01:28:48.880 --> 01:28:51.639
Ask.


01:28:53.920 --> 01:28:56.679
You don't look like him.


01:28:57.680 --> 01:29:03.839
Any suit can play the CEO
for shareholders and the media.


01:29:04.000 --> 01:29:08.239
Our founder isn't a businessman.


01:29:08.400 --> 01:29:11.879
- He has no interest in fame.
- Too bad.


01:29:12.040 --> 01:29:15.559
- That was some performance.
- Who said it was a performance?


01:29:17.560 --> 01:29:21.439
Our founder is a scientist, an innovator.


01:29:21.600 --> 01:29:25.479
He's very particular about those
he invites to work with him,


01:29:25.640 --> 01:29:29.439
especially when it comes to the most
important hiring decision he's ever made.


01:29:29.600 --> 01:29:32.759
Important enough to kill for?


01:29:36.480 --> 01:29:39.839
What makes you think he's dead?


01:30:25.240 --> 01:30:27.559
While searching for the cure,


01:30:27.720 --> 01:30:31.239
we stumbled upon
something far more powerful.


01:30:36.640 --> 01:30:39.679
Rapid cell regeneration...


01:30:43.440 --> 01:30:46.199
..in a pill.


01:30:48.200 --> 01:30:52.519
It eradicates the virus
and other stubborn mutations.


01:30:52.680 --> 01:30:57.479
- The magic bullet.
- The gift of life for millions.


01:31:02.080 --> 01:31:08.679
Such a breakthrough
creates unanticipated dilemmas.


01:31:10.560 --> 01:31:13.279
Too great for any one man to bear.


01:31:17.560 --> 01:31:20.879
People are gonna need this product,


01:31:21.040 --> 01:31:24.319
and we can only make so much at a time.


01:31:24.480 --> 01:31:27.959
Tough decisions are gonna have to be
made by a wise administrator,


01:31:28.120 --> 01:31:32.079
someone who combines
a listening disposition


01:31:32.240 --> 01:31:35.599
with attention to detail


01:31:35.760 --> 01:31:39.599
and compassion for her fellow man.


01:31:42.760 --> 01:31:46.719
If you are still interested...


01:32:37.240 --> 01:32:39.639
Il est revenu.


01:32:45.480 --> 01:32:47.999
He is...


01:32:50.840 --> 01:32:52.879
..risen.
